WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.692
These are the main habits from Module 11.

00:00:02.692 --> 00:00:06.007
Use CTEs to name logical stages.

00:00:06.007 --> 00:00:12.072
Keep row grain explicit. Use windows when you need context without losing detail.

00:00:12.072 --> 00:00:16.017
Treat ORDER BY as part of the analytical definition.

00:00:16.017 --> 00:00:18.667
Write frame boundaries when they matter.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:22.612
And choose ranking functions based on the meaning of ties.

00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:28.152
Connect this idea to a hospital ranking visits and identifying readmissions.

00:00:28.152 --> 00:00:33.602
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:33.602 --> 00:00:41.352
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.352 --> 00:00:47.332
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:47.332 --> 00:00:53.120
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
